{
  "0": "tune_batch_size: Increase batch size modestly, around 2x, while holding learning rate and other settings fixed. Larger batches may stabilize noisy sequence gradients and improve macro validation HR@10. This is an untested direction; the baseline provides no evidence yet about the best batch size.",
  "1": "tune_lr_batch_scheduler: Pair a modest batch-size increase with a smaller proportional learning-rate increase and a brief warmup followed by cosine decay across the configured training horizon. This may improve early optimization while allowing finer late-stage ranking updates. The five-epoch smoke output does not establish convergence or justify shortening training.",
  "2": "tune_num_layers: Add one SASRec transformer block while keeping embedding width, heads, loss, and optimization unchanged. Additional depth may capture higher-order item transitions and improve macro validation HR@10. Update the predictor writer to reconstruct the trained depth consistently.",
  "3": "tune_num_heads: Increase attention heads to the next modest count that divides the existing embedding width, holding depth and total width fixed. More heads may capture distinct sequential relationships and improve macro validation HR@10 without increasing embedding capacity. Update the predictor writer to load the matching head configuration."
}
